    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s name honors Pleasant Warren, the first member who gave the community its original identity.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://pleasanthilltexas.org/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In its early days, Pleasant Hill hosted two general stores, a blacksmith shop, and a saloon, serving the local ranching community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/pleasant-hill-tx-houston-county"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Pleasant Hill sits three and a half miles northwest of Linden on FM 1399, just north of the Anderson County line.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
